# BlindPath AI – Intelligent Walking Path Assistant

### AI-Powered Smart Navigation and Obstacle Detection System for Visually Impaired People

<p align="center">
  <b>Making Walking Safer Through Artificial Intelligence and Computer Vision</b>
</p>

---

## 📌 Project Overview

BlindPath AI is an Artificial Intelligence and Computer Vision-based intelligent walking assistance system designed to help visually impaired people navigate their surroundings more safely and independently.

The system uses a camera to capture real-time environmental information and applies AI-based object detection to identify obstacles, potholes, stairs, vehicles, pedestrians and other potential hazards.

It provides voice-based alerts to inform users about nearby obstacles and potential dangers.

The main objective is to improve independent mobility through affordable AI-powered assistive technology.

## 🎯 Problem Statement

Visually impaired people face difficulties identifying obstacles and navigating unfamiliar environments.

Traditional GPS navigation applications provide location-based directions but cannot reliably identify immediate physical obstacles.

BlindPath AI aims to address this problem through real-time obstacle detection, hazard identification, distance estimation and voice assistance.

## 🚀 Key Features

- **AI Object Detection:** Detects people, vehicles, chairs, walls and other objects.
- **Pothole Detection:** Identifies potholes and damaged walking surfaces.
- **Obstacle Detection:** Identifies obstacles in the user's walking direction.
- **Distance Estimation:** Estimates the distance between the camera and detected obstacles.
- **Voice Assistance:** Provides real-time spoken warnings.
- **Risk Analysis:** Evaluates potential walking hazards.
- **Direction-Based Alerts:** Provides left, right and front obstacle warnings.
- **GPS Hazard Mapping:** Displays reported dangerous locations.
- **Emergency Assistance:** Supports emergency contact functionality.

